invariant: INV-25
file: srv_parser_ext.c
catches: srv_test
reason: the wire record_size_limit counts the inner content-type byte
  (RFC 8449 §4), so a parser that stores it unchanged reports one byte
  more plaintext than the client accepts. srv_handshake.c takes the
  smaller of that value and CH_TX_PT into t->peer_limit, which session.h
  defines as the largest plaintext the peer accepts, so the error lands
  on the send path and shows only against a client that advertises, and
  only at the boundary. The first implementation of this file stored the
  wire value and its own test asserted the wire value back, so the two
  agreed and both were wrong; this mutant is what stops that pair
  returning.

--- old
    p->ch->record_size_limit = (uint16_t)(limit - 1);
--- new
    // The value is a record size limit, so store what the client sent.
    p->ch->record_size_limit = limit;
